# arizona-suite-scratch-io: checkc.icn/fncs1.icn open a relative-path scratch file for real;
# test_icon_arizona_suite.sh never isolates each run's cwd, so it lands here every run.
/foo.baz

# ⛔⭐ THE ICON SCRATCH NAMES -- ALL FOUR, ROOT-ANCHORED, AND THE ASYMMETRY IS THE LESSON (hq_I measured it
# 2026-09-13, hq_B landed it). This list carried `tmp1` (since the initial commit) and `/tmp3` (2026-08-30)
# and NOT tmp2, NOT tmp4 -- while corpus/packages/icon/{arizona,jcon}_tests write all four: io.icn opens
# tmp1/tmp2 "w" and iobig.icn testio()s tmp3/tmp4. hq_I's sitting: a stray 400KB tmp4 left by a suite run
# they did not make turned their handoff banner ⛔ FAILURE on a sitting whose work was entirely pushed.
# ⭐ hq_I'S SENTENCE, WHICH IS THE REUSABLE HALF: an ignore list that covers SOME of a generated set is worse
# than one that covers none, because the covered members train you to believe the set is handled. tmp1 and
# tmp3 being ignored is exactly why nobody looked for tmp2 and tmp4.
# ⛔ AND IT IS WORSE THAN A NUISANCE IN ONE SPECIFIC DIRECTION: handoff_status.sh says "commit them" about
# untracked output, and the obvious reading is to COMMIT a 400KB generated artifact. tmp3 was committed by
# accident once already and the ceo deleted it.
# ⭐ WHAT THESE LINES ARE FOR, AND WHAT THEY ARE NOT: the SUITES no longer write here -- test_icon_all_rungs
# runs from ICN_SCRATCH (2026-08-30) and test_icon_arizona_suite snapshots its test dirs and deletes what
# appeared (2026-09-04). These four cover the HAND RUN, a human grading a program from the repo root, which
# is a mess and not a defect. ⛔ THE DEFECT -- a suite writing into the source tree again -- must NOT be
# silenced by them, and is not: test_gate_icon_scratch_names_are_not_tracked.sh is the instrument that still
# sees it, because an ignored name is invisible to git status BY DESIGN and that is the whole hazard here.
/tmp1
/tmp2
/tmp3
/tmp4
